hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"241","We are Abu Musa, we are Abu Muawiyah, we are Al-Amash. Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Ibn Fudayl told us. H. Salam bin Junada, Waki’ told us. H. Ali bin Hajar, Issa bin Yunus, told us. H. Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, Ibn Idris, told us. H Abu Musa told us, Abdullah bin Dawud, all of them, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: My aunt Maimunah told me, she said: “I approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to wash him due to impurity.” She said: “So he washed his palms.” Two or three times, then he inserted his right hand into the vessel, poured it over his private parts, washed it with his left hand, then hit the ground with his left hand. He rubbed it vigorously, then performed his ablution for prayer, then poured three handfuls of water on his head, filling his palms, then washed the rest of his body, then He stepped down from that position and washed his feet, then I brought him the handkerchief and he straightened it.” This is the wording of the hadith of Isa bin Yunus, and he said in the report of Ibn Fudayl: “He started to wipe off the water,” and Ibn Idris also said: “Then a handkerchief was brought.” He refused to accept it, and began to shake off the water.” Some of them add to others in the text of the hadith."
